<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import SocketsChatDemo from "$ui/demos/sockets/SocketsChatDemo.abide"
  import ForAwaitDemo from "$ui/demos/sockets/ForAwaitDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Sockets</h1>
  <p class="lead"><strong><code>socket</code> = <a href="/channel"><code>channel</code></a> + transport + per-room authorization.</strong> The pub/sub core, the rooms, and the reactive read surface are all the channel primitive; a socket adds the WebSocket mux, the <code>clientPublish</code> mediator, and the <code>middleware</code> that authorizes each subscribe and publish. The client imports the <em>same</em> <code>socketsChat</code> the server does: this demo <strong>subscribes by iterating it</strong> (<code>for await (const m of socketsChat)</code>, over the WS mux), derives its status from the socket's reactive probes (<code>pending()</code> / <code>refreshing()</code> / <code>error()</code>), and publishes two ways: from the <strong>server</strong> (a POST RPC that calls <code>socket.publish</code>, arriving with <code>via: "server"</code>) and from the <strong>client</strong> (the isomorphic <code>socketsChat.publish(...)</code>, admitted by <code>clientPublish</code> — whose function form <em>is</em> the permission, mediating the untrusted message by stamping <code>via: "client"</code> and dropping empty text). Both feed one live log; "Clear local log" resets it.</p>
  <Demo id="socket-chat" title="<code>socket()</code> — iterate (<code>for await</code>) + <code>publish()</code> from server &amp; client" server="src/server/sockets/socketsChat.ts" client="src/ui/demos/sockets/SocketsChatDemo.abide" tab="server">
    <SocketsChatDemo />
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>One import, both sides: <code>socketsChat</code> is the same <code>Socket&lt;ChatMessage&gt;</code> the server holds, consumed here in the browser as an <code>AsyncIterable</code>, published to with <code>.publish()</code>, and probed with <code>.pending()</code> / <code>.refreshing()</code> / <code>.error()</code>. The status line is those probes — there is no connection bookkeeping to hand-roll.</p>
  </aside>
  <Demo id="socket-forawait" title="<code>{'{'}#for await message of socketsChat{'}'}</code>" server="src/server/sockets/socketsChat.ts" client="src/ui/demos/sockets/ForAwaitDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <ForAwaitDemo />
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>The template block <code>{'{'}#for await message of socketsChat{'}'}</code> <em>is</em> the subscription — it rides the multiplexed WebSocket at <code>/__abide/sockets</code> transparently (one connection carries every named socket), appending each message as it arrives. No raw connection, no frames.</p>
    <p>The socket keeps a <code>tail</code> of recent messages, so reloading this page replays them immediately — no re-publish needed.</p>
    <p>Beyond iterating, a socket carries the reactive probe surface — <code>live()</code> (latest message), <code>chunks()</code> (tail transcript), plus <code>pending</code>/<code>refreshing</code>/<code>error</code>. They have their own page: <a href="/sockets/probes">Socket probes</a>.</p>
  </aside>
</main>
